# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# THE DEPLOY PROCEDURE, because getting it wrong is expensive (see below):
#
#     cd web
#     vercel build --prod              # runs the full prebuild gate locally
#     vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod  # uploads .vercel/output only
#
# Build LOCALLY and ship the output. The prebuild gate runs `check-css` against
# ../skills and `db-gate` against ../data, and only a local build has those.
#
# TWO WAYS THIS GOES WRONG, both hit on 2026-08-25:
#
#  1. `cd web && vercel --prod` (no --prebuilt) uploads 38 files — web/ alone —
#     and the Vercel-side build dies on
#     `ENOENT: /vercel/skills/design-language/assets/style.css`.
#
#  2. `vercel --prod` from the repo root uploads ~650 MB across thousands of
#     files. The CLI aborts the upload, and the attempts burn the account's
#     free-tier file quota: `api-upload-free`, "more than 5000, try again in
#     24 hours". A wrong deploy command costs a day, so read this first.
#
# The project's Root Directory is `.` and there is no package.json there, so a
# Vercel-side build cannot detect Next.js either way. Prebuilt is the flow.
#
# The ignores below only matter if someone deploys from the root anyway. They
# take that upload from ~650 MB to ~26 MB.

# 117 MB of raw harvest payloads. The canonical ledger is data/signals/**.jsonl;
# raw/ is the provenance archive and nothing in the build path opens it.
data/raw/

# A gitignored projection, rebuilt from the journal by web/scripts/db-gate.mjs
# inside prebuild. Shipping a prebuilt one would let a stale store reach
# production — the exact failure the gate exists to prevent.
data/register.db

node_modules
web/node_modules
web/.next
.git
